Volt GUI (Vulkan GPU Control Panel & Settings Manager)

volt-gui is an open-source graphical control panel and Vulkan implicit layer
(VK_LAYER_VOLT_settings) for Vulkan games on Linux.

It acts as a driver-agnostic alternative to AMD Adrenaline or NVIDIA Settings,
giving you fine-grained control over frame limiting, anisotropic filtering,
texture LOD bias, display resolutions, and GPU selection.

Usage:
  - Open Volt GUI from your desktop application launcher or run: volt-gui
  - In Steam launch options, add: volt -- %command%
  - In terminal / custom scripts, run: volt -- ./game
